\begin{table*}[t]
  \centering
  \caption{Ten-seed OU--III wave-direction results over the final \SI{900}{s}, against the generator azimuth of each record. The propagation axis is defined modulo \SI{180}{\degree}, so $|\Delta\theta|$ is the absolute axial error of the circular-mean estimate and $\theta_{\mathrm{RMSE}}$ is the sample-wise axial RMS error. \emph{Sense} is a genuine correctness rate: the estimator's directed propagation vector, with the vessel heading removed, scored against the physical propagation direction of the record, which is the v1.2.1 incident propagation azimuth. \emph{Unresolved} is the share below the confidence and amplitude thresholds. The FORWARD/BACKWARD classes the estimator exports are relative to the axis representative it happens to return and invert under a \SI{180}{\degree} heading change, so they are not scored here. Entries are mean $\pm$ sample standard deviation over the seed triplets.}
